WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.070
- Well wait, speaking of Dan's dad,

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.320
he told a story about
Dan the first time he was

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.153
at our show.

00:00:05.153 --> 00:00:05.986
So let's see that.

00:00:05.986 --> 00:00:06.819
Yeah.

00:00:06.819 --> 00:00:08.280
- When my son was 15

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:13.280
and he was going to come
with us in Los Angeles.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.136
We went down for the premiere.

00:00:15.136 --> 00:00:15.969
- Yeah.

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:17.340
- Of the movie.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.060
And the night before the premiere he said

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.480
he was on the phone call with
his friend back in Toronto

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.070
and they said, "Well, what's going on?"

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.976
He said, "Well, I'm going to
the premiere of "American Pie"

00:00:28.976 --> 00:00:30.930
tomorrow night with my folks."

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.950
And the friend said, "Oh,
don't see it with your folks."

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.659
(audience laughs)

00:00:37.659 --> 00:00:38.492
- Did you not?

00:00:38.492 --> 00:00:39.325
Did you not go?

00:00:39.325 --> 00:00:40.158
- No.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:42.263
Absolutely not.

00:00:42.263 --> 00:00:44.130
- [Kelly] Oh my God.
- Absolutely not, no.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.030
I called a friend.

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:47.340
They had just seen like an
advanced screening of it

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.280
and said, "Run in the opposite direction

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.750
of wherever your parents are

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.430
in relation to that film."

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:54.263
And I did.

00:00:54.263 --> 00:00:56.760
And I have yet to see it with them.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.320
I did end up seeing it.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.390
For most of my high school life,

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.060
people thought the movie was
like a biography of my life.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.040
- Yeah.
(audience laughs)

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.440
That is unfortunate.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.259
- Which is really unfortunate.

00:01:09.259 --> 00:01:10.092
- That's unfortunate.

00:01:10.092 --> 00:01:11.250
- Because I would've
killed to have had a life

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.178
that interesting.

00:01:12.178 --> 00:01:13.609
(audience laughs)

00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:15.390
- And why apple pie? Yeah.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.370
- I don't even know about the
ingredients of an apple pie,

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:18.897
but that's a whole other conversation.

00:01:18.897 --> 00:01:20.940
(audience laughs)

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.200
- I think my mother's the opposite.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.940
I would be fine I think in that scenario.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:25.590
I think my mother would die.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:26.501
- Okay.

00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:27.334
You would be fine.
- I'm very open.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:28.167
I'm very open.

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:29.190
I will talk to my mother

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:31.050
about anything.
- [Dan] Everything.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:33.750
- So will my sister
and my mother hates it.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:34.620
- [Dan] Wow.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.270
- Like with a capital H.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.170
- [Dan] Okay.
- Yeah.

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:39.120
- I don't have that dynamic.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.350
My dad is very sweet.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.120
But no, there was no...

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:42.960
- I have no problem.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.280
I could talk about anything with her.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.113
- [Dan] Oh great.

00:01:45.113 --> 00:01:46.110
- Like literally anything.

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:48.504
And I try, but she is like,

00:01:48.504 --> 00:01:50.190
your mouth is moving, stop.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:51.023
- She's the opposite

00:01:51.023 --> 00:01:52.290
of what this movie was to me.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.150
- Yeah, she's not into it.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.100
So I would've gone to the premiere.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:58.680
Anyway, your dad's in a
(beep) cool, awesome movie.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.537
I would've gone.

00:01:59.537 --> 00:02:00.370
- Yeah, he was.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.530
Yeah, you know, it's a weird thing

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.780
to grow up watching your
dad just hand out porn

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:04.944
to some other kid.

00:02:04.944 --> 00:02:07.777
(audience laughs)

